    edibility: "edible-with-caution",
    preparation: "A prized wild onion (a favorite of forager-chef Hank Shaw): the small bulb, leaves and pink flower umbels are used raw or cooked exactly like a cultivated onion - grilled, pickled, chopped into eggs, or as a garnish. Harvest a few from a clump and leave the rest.",
    cautions: "MANDATORY ONION-SMELL TEST. Before eating any part, crush the leaf or bulb: a true Allium releases an unmistakable onion/garlic smell. If it does NOT smell of onion, discard it - deadly death camas grows in the same ground, has a similar papery-coated bulb, and has killed people who mistook it for wild onion. Confirm smell on every single harvest, not just the patch.",
